  "body": "This changes addresses a compat issue with `ConicGradient`.\n\nThe current implementations on Safari and Firefox align the angle with CSS. Chrome's implementation and the current spec doesn't. An example of the problem is described [here](https://twitter.com/AdrianBeceDev/status/1561682684031782919) with this [code](https://codepen.io/AdrianBece/pen/qBovjNg).\n\nThis changes updates the spec to match CSS, i.e., we describe Canvas' ConicGradient angle as the same as CSS's `conic-gradient()` angle.\n\nThe original argument for adjusting the angle was found in some code review as *\"since all angles in canvas is related to the x-axis, rotate the conic gradient by 90 degrees such that the gradient starts from x-axis.\"* I have no idea what this means, so I decided to ignore it and align CSS and all 3 UAs, which makes sense to me.\n\nChrome's implementation is being changed [here](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/3846302) ([bug](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1355539)) together with the relevant [WPT tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/35559).\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8213/canvas.html\" title=\"Last updated on Aug 22, 2022, 9:30 PM UTC (dd7f143)\">/canvas.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8213/22d8cdb...dd7f143/canvas.html\" title=\"Last updated on Aug 22, 2022, 9:30 PM UTC (dd7f143)\">diff</a> )",
